      "message": "While `len + 1 \u003d\u003d 0` relies on well-defined unsigned integer wrap-around and works perfectly on our target architectures (where `unsigned int` is 32-bit), using `len \u003d\u003d UINT32_MAX` or `len \u003d\u003d 0xFFFFFFFF` is generally considered more explicit and avoids any theoretical issues on exotic architectures where `int` might be wider than 32 bits.",
